@meta
id: 13-18
title: Match here, land there
chapter: 13
type: lesson
skills: regex-zs-ze
par: 38
minutes: 7
vscode: Ctrl+D on LEGACY_ and then deselect the two you did not mean
open: refund.provider.ts

@brief
The error registry has dropped its `LEGACY_` prefixes. Four `throw`
statements in this provider still use the old codes — strip `LEGACY_`
from each of them, so `'LEGACY_REFUND_DECLINED'` becomes
`'REFUND_DECLINED'` and so on.

The prefix appears in two other places that are *not* error codes: the
`LEGACY_REFUND_LIMIT` constant, imported at the top and used in a
comparison. Those keep their names.

So the context is `exception('` and the thing to delete is `LEGACY_`.
Every pattern you have written so far has landed at the start of its
match, which here would be the `e` of `exception` — nine characters
from where you want to be. This lesson is the fix, and it is the one
part of vim's regex that no other tool has.

@keys
| `\zs` | "start the match here" — everything before it is checked but not matched |
| `/exception('\zsLEGACY_` | find `LEGACY_`, but only after `exception('`, and land on the `L` |
| `dgn` | delete the next match — and the match is only what came after `\zs` |
| `.` | delete the next one too |

@hints
The pattern has to mention `exception('` to rule out the constant, but
the cursor and the deletion need to start at `LEGACY_`. Vim lets one
pattern say both.
--
`\zs` marks where the match begins. Put it after the context and before
the thing you want. The cursor lands on the `L`, and `gn` selects only
`LEGACY_`.
--
`/exception('\zsLEGACY_` `Enter`, then `dgn`, then `.` three times.

@solution
/exception('\zsLEGACY_<Enter>  dgn  .  .  .  :wq<Enter>

Thirty-three keystrokes, and the constant was never at risk.

`\zs` — "zero-width start" — splits a pattern into two parts: what must
be there, and what counts as the match. The text before `\zs` has to
be present for the pattern to succeed, but it is not part of the
result. So the cursor lands after it, highlighting starts after it,
and — the part that matters most — `gn` selects only what follows it.
`dgn` deleted seven characters, not sixteen.

That is what makes `\zs` more than a landing trick. Chapter 11's `cgn`
and `dgn` change or delete *the match*, and until now the match was
the whole pattern. With `\zs`, the match is the part you want to edit
and the rest is context that has to be true. Any find-and-change job
that needs a condition on what comes before — change this only after
that — is one `\zs` away from being a `cgn` and a row of dots.

This was written in the default dialect on purpose. Under `\v` the
round bracket in `exception(` would have needed a backslash and the
pattern would have been `\vexception\('\zsLEGACY_` — longer, for
nothing. Very magic is the better default; it is not a law. When the
literal text is full of brackets and the pattern has no quantifiers,
the plain dialect is shorter. Pick per pattern.

@start refund.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { LEGACY_REFUND_LIMIT } from './refund.constants';
import { RefundRepository } from './refund.repository';
import { OrderRepository } from '../order/order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class RefundProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(RefundRepository) protected refundRepository: RefundRepository,
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(args: { id: string }) {
    const refund = await this.refundRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.id } });

    if (!refund) {
      throw exception('LEGACY_REFUND_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return refund;
  }

  public async create(args: { orderId: string; amount: number }) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.orderId } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    if (args.amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('LEGACY_REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    const requiresApproval = args.amount > LEGACY_REFUND_LIMIT;

    return this.refundRepository.create({
      values: { orderId: order.id, amount: args.amount, status: requiresApproval ? 'PENDING_APPROVAL' : 'PENDING' },
    });
  }

  public async settle(args: { id: string }) {
    const refund = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (refund.status === 'SETTLED') {
      throw exception('LEGACY_REFUND_ALREADY_SETTLED');
    }

    const result = await this.paymentService.refund(refund.orderId, refund.amount);

    if (!result.ok) {
      throw exception('LEGACY_REFUND_DECLINED');
    }

    return this.refundRepository.update({ where: { id: refund.id }, values: { status: 'SETTLED' } });
  }
}

@expected refund.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { LEGACY_REFUND_LIMIT } from './refund.constants';
import { RefundRepository } from './refund.repository';
import { OrderRepository } from '../order/order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class RefundProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(RefundRepository) protected refundRepository: RefundRepository,
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(args: { id: string }) {
    const refund = await this.refundRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.id } });

    if (!refund) {
      throw exception('REFUND_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return refund;
  }

  public async create(args: { orderId: string; amount: number }) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.orderId } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    if (args.amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    const requiresApproval = args.amount > LEGACY_REFUND_LIMIT;

    return this.refundRepository.create({
      values: { orderId: order.id, amount: args.amount, status: requiresApproval ? 'PENDING_APPROVAL' : 'PENDING' },
    });
  }

  public async settle(args: { id: string }) {
    const refund = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (refund.status === 'SETTLED') {
      throw exception('REFUND_ALREADY_SETTLED');
    }

    const result = await this.paymentService.refund(refund.orderId, refund.amount);

    if (!result.ok) {
      throw exception('REFUND_DECLINED');
    }

    return this.refundRepository.update({ where: { id: refund.id }, values: { status: 'SETTLED' } });
  }
}
